This package is a vendored subset of the WebView2 COM binding from Wails v3.

    Source:  github.com/wailsapp/wails/v3 v3.0.0-beta.6
             internal/webview2/pkg/edge          -> internal/webview2
             internal/webview2/pkg/combridge     -> internal/webview2/combridge
             internal/webview2/webviewloader     -> internal/webview2/loader
             internal/webview2/internal/w32      -> internal/webview2/w32
    License: MIT
    Copyright (c) 2018-Present Lea Anthony

It is vendored rather than imported because Wails places it under internal/,
which Go's import rules put out of reach of this module. No new third-party code
enters the binary as a result: golang.org/x/sys and github.com/jchv/go-winloader
were already dependencies, the latter indirectly through Wails itself.

Vendored from pkg/edge and not from pkg/webview2. The latter is generated code
that nothing in Wails imports, and it flattens COM inheritance: an interface's
vtable is declared as IUnknown plus its own methods, omitting every inherited
slot. Because ICoreWebView2Environment10 derives from ICoreWebView2Environment9,
seventeen slots are missing there and calls land on unrelated methods.

Local changes:

  ICoreWebView2CookieManager.GetCookies         (corrected in place)
      Now takes the completion handler the IDL declares. Upstream passed an
      out-parameter where the handler belongs, which the runtime dereferences as
      an interface pointer and faults on.

  Recoverable view creation                     (changed, chromium.go)
      CreateCoreWebView2ControllerCompleted, the GetCoreWebView2 failure inside
      initializeController, and Embed's pre-pump failures now return instead of
      exiting the process. WebView2 aborts creation with E_ABORT whenever the
      host window is destroyed first, which is what closing a session window
      before it finishes opening does; upstream calls errorCallback, which
      os.Exit(1)s, so the whole application went down with the window. Embed's
      nested pump gained a failure exit and Embed now returns false, the path
      its caller already tests.

  Chromium.ProfileName                          (added field, chromium.go)
      When set, the controller is created through CreateControllerWithProfile so
      the view gets its own cookie jar. One Chromium per browser window, all
      sharing a DataPath, is how callers open several accounts at once.

  ICoreWebView2GetCookiesCompletedHandler.go    (added)
      The handler type the corrected GetCookies needs.

  profile.go                                    (added)
      ICoreWebView2Environment10 and ICoreWebView2ControllerOptions, which name a
      profile at controller creation. Absent upstream.

  environment.go                                (added)
      Profile-name validation, and why environments are not created directly.

  navigation.go, navigation_handlers.go         (added)
      Source, title, history and new-window plumbing for a URL bar and its
      back/forward buttons.

  download.go                                   (added)
      ICoreWebView2_4 and the DownloadStarting event, so a host can refuse a
      download rather than take WebView2's default of a transfer into the
      profile's folder and a flyout over the page. Absent upstream.

Vtable slot layouts in the added files were derived from the WebView2 IDL, at
v3/internal/webview2/scripts/WebView2.1.0.2592.51.idl in the Wails repository,
rather than inferred. A wrong slot does not fail loudly, so profile_test.go
exercises the corrected and added interfaces against the real runtime and
asserts that two profiles cannot see each other's cookies.
